<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela oil minister defends use of gov't planes.</title>
<headline>Venezuela oil minister defends use of gov't planes.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's Energy and Mines Minister Erwin Arrieta defended his use of government aircraft as a necessary part of his work and rejected allegations that he had wasted taxpayers' money on pleasure trips.</p>
<p>&quot;Absolutely every flight taken by me has been for work commitments,&quot; Arrieta told a Congressional commission studying accusations that officials have used state oil company Petroleos de Venezuela (PDVSA) aircraft, boats and houses for holidays.</p>
</text>
